<!--Post: 10128--><!--Time: 1109779367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10128"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KWCH 12 Eyewitness News <BR>Monday, February 28, 2005 <BR> <BR>Officer recalls BTK first murders   <BR>He had just been promoted to lieutenant when Jack Watkins got the call that&#39;s haunted him for 31 years. He was the first Wichita policeman inside the Otero&#39;s where four people were tortured and murdered. For decades, Watkins has struggled with what he saw. Now he&#39;s relieved to learn BTK is no longer killing people. <BR> <BR><b>&#34;The first thing I seen was this little boy… it still bothers me. This little guy was sitting in the chair. Had multiple paper bags pulled over his head- rope around his neck. He&#39;s tied to this chair.&#34;</b> <BR> <BR>Nine-year old Joseph Otero had been strangled. In the bedroom two more bodies. <BR> <BR>&#34;I see a full size bed and a woman laying across it and she appeared to be dead. She was bound with rope.&#34; Watkins remembers. <BR> <BR>At the foot of the bed, Joseph Otero was tied up same as his wife. <BR> <BR>&#34;That&#39;s the next thing that haunted me is how did someone have that much control over people that&#39;s had little kids apparently.&#34; <BR> <BR>Then Watkins made it to the basement. <BR> <BR>&#34;The first thing I seen was a young girl hanging from the cross members of the basement &#40;ceiling&#41; half dressed and half nude.&#34; <BR> <BR>After 31 years of dead ends, the haunting of Jack Watkins is near an end. <BR> <BR>&#34;There is a closure. It&#39;s not one of those things you&#39;re just going to shelve and forget it because you don&#39;t forget it.&#34; Said Watkins.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10128-->
<!--Post: 10129--><!--Time: 1109779584-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10129"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 8:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If we had known that he was tied to a chair, we may not have been so skeptical of connecting Kathryn Bright to BTK. If true...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10129-->
<!--Post: 10193--><!--Time: 1109807525-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10193"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 3:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LE released very little info on the crime scenes, the absolute minimum when you think about it, so I think a lot of surprising things will come out at the trial.  I&#39;m not so sure that I want to hear all of the awful details anyway. <BR> <BR>If what Officer Watkins says is the truth, then LE was releasing some misleading info -- they&#39;d been saying all along that Joseph II was found lying on the floor and that there was a chair brought into the room, where it was suggested that BTK would have sat while Joseph died. This may have been intentional, since &#34;Denny the Dog Catcher&#34; wrote to LE and media to correct misinformation before.  Maybe LE has released other incorrect details in  <BR>order to provoke further communication from DR? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10193-->
<!--Post: 10194--><!--Time: 1109807600-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10194"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 3:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If there is a trial, I should say... with any luck DR will plead guilty to something and they can get the sentencing over with quickly.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10194-->
<!--Post: 10358--><!--Time: 1109912003-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10358"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paper bags means he didnt want to see the boys&#39; face as he died. I think that explains btk did feel awkward about that killing. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10358-->
<!--Post: 10423--><!--Time: 1109941125-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10423"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The point that I&#39;m trying to make is that BTK stated in his letter that Joe Jr. was laying on his back as opposed to lieutenant Jack Watkins claiming that Joe Jr. was <b>sitting in a chair.</b> <BR> <BR>Below is an excerpt from BTK&#39;s letter: <BR> <BR>Joseph: <BR>        Position: In the east bedroom <b>laying on his back </b>pointed in eastern <BR>        Bondage: Blind cord. <BR>        Garrote: Three hoods; white T-shirt, white plastic bag,another T-shirt <BR>        Clothes line cord with clove-hitch. <BR>        Death: Suffocation once, stranglation &#40;sp&#41;-suffocation with the old bag  <BR>        Clothes: Brown pants, yellow-brown stripe T-shirt <BR>        Comments: His radio is blaring  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m just wondering, which version is true?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10423-->
<!--Post: 10556--><!--Time: 1110000981-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10556"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Next<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Next<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why are you calling him dog catcher? He was smart enough to get away with murder for 30 years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10556-->
<!--Post: 10576--><!--Time: 1110029848-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10576"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 5:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->True, Next. <BR>But he was stupid enough to keep communicating. <BR>Such a pompous jerk, he could not shut up. <BR>It feel sorta good to belittle him, by calling him Dog Catcher. <BR>&#40;not saying being a dog catcher is a bad thing. but it does not take being a rocket scientist to do that&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10576-->
<!--Post: 10588--><!--Time: 1110037852-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10588"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 7:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Next...its actually &#34;DENNY THE DOG CATCHER&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10588-->
<!--Post: 10593--><!--Time: 1110045139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 9:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree Audrey! The general consensus at home is that everybody hopes that he will plead guilty - and spare the families another year of agony. I&#39;m hopeing that his minister has mentioned this to him. On the other hand, we all know how much he craved attention. Hopefully he is medicated now, and grew some compassion. If not, god please help the victims families, friends and neighbors get through a trial.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10593-->
<!--Post: 10993--><!--Time: 1110336483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10993"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 6:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I feel that I&#39;m being ghoulish about this, but what happened to JoeII has a lot to do with whether BTK acted alone or with a partner, as there would be no question if he can be linked to the Michael Williams shooting.   <BR> <BR>A policeman, trained to be observant at a crime scene &#40; as if you could erase that one from your memory&#41; remembers JoeII sitting in a chair with paper bags over his head. BTK, in an attempt to PROVE that he was at the scene, says laying on his back with t-shirts and a plastic bag. Did someone move him after BTK last saw him, and maybe put a paper bag over his head? Was there a reason to put emphasis on the son? <BR> <BR>I can remember when it occured, there was a lot of talk about the Michael Williams shooting and why it seemed that the family wanted it &#34;swept under the rug&#34; and seemed to get what they wanted.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10993-->
<!--Post: 11035--><!--Time: 1110384102-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11035"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bojo<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bojo<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 8:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The crime scene drawing also shows him lying on the ground.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11035-->
</table></td></tr></table>
